{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514307-oubliette","id":1514307,"title":"Oubliette","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-09T07:49:33-07:00","id":1514307,"title":"Oubliette","content":"So, now on today's topic I wanted to discuss with you fellow members of this honored forum about the Obtenebration power Oubliette as it's detailed in the DAV20.<br /> <br /> As many of you are probably aware, this is a level 8 Obtenebration power that allows the Lasombra (or whoever attained such a mastery of this Discipline) to imprison someone in the Abyss of his/her own soul. This is probably one of the best Obtenebration powers in my opinion, but there's some discussion about how effective it should be allowed to be. In the discussion that happened the other day with another fellow vampire fan, this friend of mine said she believed this power shouldn't be able to imprison &quot;an all-powerful Cainite&quot;, that means she thinks a powerful being like an Antediluvian should somehow be immune to this kind of power, but then I argued that I think it's up to discussion, there's no such limitation in the power's text, so in thesis the vampire should be able to even imprison a being like Tremere or Ashur, Saulot, etc, if he somehow managed to have a &quot;good roll&quot;. <br /> <br /> Another topic that this powers brings, I already mentioned in my first paragraph here, is the idea that this prison isn't really in the Abyss itself, but rather in the &quot;darkness of the user's soul&quot;, this is something that is mentioned in the text, specifically in this passage: &quot;A vampire may maintain only one Oubliette at a time (which can only contain one victim at a time), which leads some Cainite philosophers to argue that it is a prison inside the vampire herself and not some distant Abyssal nightmare.&quot; (p. 231, DAV20). Something I find very interesting, if not mind-blowing. <br /> <br /> So, in your opinion should this power's prison be so powerful as to allow one to imprison &quot;goodlike beings&quot; as I cited in the example and what do you think is this prison in itself, is it the Abyss or inside the vampire himself as if perhaps in his own soul, etc? What implications do you think it might bring to the table?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T09:35:50-07:00","id":1514311,"title":"","content":"The &quot;original&quot; version is from Guide to the Sabbat ('99 edition) said the same about the Oubliette<br /> It is important to mention, both version describes the <i>Oubliette</i> appears as a dense patch of shadow, unaffected by ambient light. No air exists in this shadow-trap, and mortals suffocate within its chilling void.<br /> And more importantly? The Oubliette vanishes instantly when touched by sunlight<br /> It is something &quot;summoned&quot;, not banishment in to the Abyss<br /> &quot;Just&quot; summoned darkness, but the darkness is from the Abyss - probably, tho' the idea of the darknes or abscence of soul also could work<br /> <br /> However?<br /> There is an Abyss Mysticism level 7 ritual called Evocation of the Oubliette from Players Guide to High Clans and/or Vampire: the Dark Ages 20th<br /> With this ritual, a mystic may reach out with grasping tendrils of Obtenebration to seize a victim and cast her into the Abyss. The tendrils may emerge from the caster\u2019s fingertips or mouth or perhaps reach from some deep shadow like the arms of a lurking beast. Regardless of their source, the end result is the same. When the oily tentacles withdraw, no trace of the victim remains.<br /> <b>System: </b>The vampire spends a full turn in concentration, focusing upon his victim and the hunger of the void. If the vampire is disturbed during this time or breaks off to attempt any other action, his player must roll Wits + Occult (difficulty 8) or suffer the effects of a botched casting as described below. On the turn following the preparation, the vampire gestures forcefully at the victim and his player spends 3 blood points. The actual attack is made with Perception + Occult (difficulty 6) and may be dodged but not parried. A failed attack means the tendrils simply close on nothing and withdraw. If the attack results in any successes, the tendrils envelop the victim and drag her into a spherical prison of emptiness within the Abyss. The mystic may recall the victim at any time for the cost of one blood point, in which case the nearest shadow disgorges its prisoner with a shuddering sigh. If the mystic does not recall the victim before a number of nights equal to his Occult score have passed, shadows disgorge the victim as near to her original location as possible. On a botched attack roll, the shadows swallow the mystic and keep him prisoner for a number of hours equal to his Obtenebration rating. After this time has elapsed, the Cainite returns to his original location and immediately enters R\u00f6tschreck. Weak-willed prisoners of this ritual may go mad as a result of their captivity. If a victim\u2019s Willpower is less than the caster\u2019s Obtenebration rating, the victim gains a derangement that lasts until cured with repeated Willpower expenditure. It is possible for vampires to drive themselves insane with a botched casting.<br /> A level 8 variant of this ritual exists called Ahriman\u2019s Beckoning. This ritual follows the same rules, save that the caster need not see the target. Instead, he may simply speak her name to the Abyss. If the victim is within a number of miles equal to the vampire\u2019s Obtenebration + Occult, the tendrils can seize her with a successful attack. It is said that the Eldest once used an even greater ritual to bring guests to his castle from distant nations, although not in recent centuries.<br /> <br /> So it is possible<br /> Or Obtenebration 9th level power, Ahriman's Demesne similarly could devour/trap someone<br /> This power allows the vampire to summon a darkness so obliviating that it extinguishes the light of life - or unlife - of any victim trapped within it. Ahriman's Demesne creates a 50-foot radius void that issues from the Cainite's hand and takes away the bodies of those it claims when it vanishes. The overwhelming darkness destroys friend and foe alike, claiming anyone unfortunate enough to be within its circumference.<br /> <b>System</b>: The player spends two points of Willpower and concentrates for three turns. During this time, the blackness billows out of the character's hand, growing to fill the area. At the end of the third turn, the player rolls Manipulation + Occult (difficulty 6). Everyone in the darkness' area suffers that many health levels of aggravated damage (not dice). After Ahriman's Demesne does its damage, it collapses, taking with it the bodies of any who died when they came in contact with the dreadful shadow.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, back to the Oubliette, yes, with a good roll, it is possible to trap &quot;an all-powerful Cainite&quot; (tho' good luck, to actually create the Oubliette around someone requires a contested Wits + Security roll against the target's Dexterity + Occult (difficulty 7 for both rolls)) but it probably would only work in a white room scenario, in an actual fight, not that sure, youwould have time or would be a 1v1 - an all-powerful Cainite have a few trick up in her sleeves<br /> And I don't think this is a bad thing; Obtenebration is something very <i>unnatural</i> even alien, like Vicissitude<br /> May cainite scholars belive, Vicissitude and Obtenebration are actually the manifestation of their respective Qliphoth, realities with different laws of physics than our own <br /> By this logic, they are on par with Chimestry's realit warping, so could and should work against &quot;an all-powerful Cainite&quot; - even mighty vampires managed to die against weaker foe after all<br /> An Antediluvian or even an old enough 4th Gen would be realistically out of your reach even on its bad day and your very lucky one with rolls tho' - even a similar power level vampire could be a problem. Why?<br /> Because Occam's razor so to speak<br /> The Lasombra Antediluvian - who basically invented Obtenebration or at least the first recorded user of it - ended the Jyhad before it started slowely and one by one Oublietteing his brothers and sisters, then the 2nd gen, and Caine if it would be remotely realistic option<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T09:37:51-07:00","id":1514312,"title":"","content":"I think it can be used as a valid resource in a situation where the Final Boss is a very powerful Elder, a Methuselah, or even an Antidiluvian, maybe even other creatures that are too strong to deal with normally, however it should be used with caution, because that would also make a battle a lot easier so my advice is that if you are going to use it against a very powerful opponent find a limitation, like that the target must be immobile or sufficiently weakened for example.<br /> <br /> As for the Roleplay question, assuming that this is even a part of the soul, depending on what he trapped in the Oubliette he can develop a connection and be affected psycho and emotionally, If he is a fallen one for example, he can have nightmares or visions of the past his past, if is a werewolf he can feel a diluited rage that may or may not interfere with his behavior, in case the target is also a Silent Strider maybe he can hear ghosts as if they were voices in his head, if he is a Formori or something corrupted by the Wyrm, so this could serve as an opening for kindred to be corrupted. Now limiting myself to vampires, if a target was a Malkavian this could establish a tenuous connection with the network of madness, if it is a toreador maybe this will make the kindred develop a similar impulse to the weakness of the clan, but with a much lower intensity, if it were a Nagaraja he might develop an urge for flesh, though he still couldn't digest it and would only have that urge. Anyway it's just an idea, it's up to you to decide how it would affect the character.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T09:42:50-07:00","id":1514313,"title":"","content":"Too scared to edit, so...<br /> There some nasty old powers that could be a problem even for an Ancient<br /> Mytherceria's 8th levele power from the 1992Players Guide to the Sabbat <b>Basilisk\u2019s Touch </b>is a good example<br /> The Kiasyd can turn victims to solid stone simply by touching them. The effects are permanent, and the only way to reverse the effect is through powerful Thaumaturgy or by another touch of the Kiasyd.<br /> <b>System: </b>This power takes effect as soon as the attacker succeeds in touching the victim and spending two points of Willpower. The victim resists with at least three successes on a Willpower roll (difficulty 8).<br /> <br /> Similar a bit to Oubliette <br /> On a good day, you could even turn an Antediluvian in to stone... with a lot of if <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T15:13:06-07:00","id":1514343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is an Abyss Mysticism level 7 ritual called Evocation of the Oubliette from Players Guide to High Clans and/or Vampire: the Dark Ages 20th </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know this ritual and if I'm not mistaken I have in the past even created a topic around here to tell how absolutely disgustingly weak (just to avoid &quot;nasty&quot; words) it is for a level 7 power. You basically give people a &quot;round-trip ticket&quot; to the Abyss, I mean WTH, the guy comes back as if basically nothing happened, in my games they have to find the way back themselves.<br /> <br /> Regarding Oubliette, at least in the DAV20 version they changed the test to something less ludicrous than &quot;security&quot; lol and it's now occult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or Obtenebration 9th level power, Ahriman's Demesne similarly could devour/trap someone </div> </div> </div>This is yet another power I have talked s%&amp;! around here in the past lol, for a level 9 power to force you to wait to deal basically less damage than an initiate mage can cause is ludicrous, I make it it &quot;instant cast&quot; in my games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lasombra Antediluvian - who basically invented Obtenebration or at least the first recorded user of it - ended the Jyhad before it started slowely and one by one Oublietteing his brothers and sisters, then the 2nd gen, and Caine if it would be remotely realistic option </div> </div> </div>One can only hold one target there (and that's the whole reason why occultists consider it possibly to mean that the cainite imprson another within his &quot;the shadows of his own soul&quot; and as you stated there's the fact that there's a test, the same kind of joke could be said about MANY powers that have the potential to be a &quot;win button&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> not that sure, youwould have time or would be a 1v1 - an all-powerful Cainite have a few trick up in her sleeves </div> </div> </div>I agree, but then again the same could be said about basically any power and at least it's an instant power, you don't need to &quot;charge&quot; like the ludicrous Ahriman's Demesne.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is that if you are going to use it against a very powerful opponent find a limitation, like that the target must be immobile or sufficiently weakened for example. </div> </div> </div>That's something I like, I mean in the actual game where it happened, the &quot;all-powerful Cainite&quot; was severely weakened before that happened, it was a conflict between two NPCs, but then later I discussed with one player about it and so was this topic born, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>System: </b>This power takes effect as soon as the attacker succeeds in touching the victim and spending two points of Willpower. The victim resists with at least three successes on a Willpower roll (difficulty 8).\u200b </div> </div> </div>This is a nice power by the way, but unfortunately somewhat easy to resist, that's why I prefer contested rolls, they're much more &quot;fair&quot; in my opinion and avoid a lot of problems like stupid powers like &quot;Paws of the Newborn Cub&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T15:28:15-07:00","id":1514344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514307-oubliette#post1514307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, now on today's topic I wanted to discuss with you fellow members of this honored forum about the Obtenebration power Oubliette as it's detailed in the DAV20.<br /> <br /> As many of you are probably aware, this is a level 8 Obtenebration power that allows the Lasombra (or whoever attained such a mastery of this Discipline) to imprison someone in the Abyss of his/her own soul. This is probably one of the best Obtenebration powers in my opinion, but there's some discussion about how effective it should be allowed to be. In the discussion that happened the other day with another fellow vampire fan, this friend of mine said she believed this power shouldn't be able to imprison &quot;an all-powerful Cainite&quot;, that means she thinks a powerful being like an Antediluvian should somehow be immune to this kind of power, but then I argued that I think it's up to discussion, there's no such limitation in the power's text, so in thesis the vampire should be able to even imprison a being like Tremere or Ashur, Saulot, etc, if he somehow managed to have a &quot;good roll&quot;.<br /> <br /> . . .<br /> <br /> So, in your opinion should this power's prison be so powerful as to allow one to imprison &quot;goodlike beings&quot; as I cited in the example and what do you think is this prison in itself, is it the Abyss or inside the vampire himself as if perhaps in his own soul, etc? What implications do you think it might bring to the table?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, it looks like Obten. is the manipulation of actual darkness, not perceived darkness, which would entail in our minds. <br /> <br /> &quot;Good-Roll&quot;, which, I'm a bit Requiem tainted that a higher-gen., can't affect a lower-gen., no matter how good they roll, but as a ST, I'd say that whichever works for the story and, eight-dots is like, 5th gen, so, that's a very powerful character in a powerful game. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T23:17:59-07:00","id":1514400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514307-oubliette?p=1514344#post1514344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, it looks like Obten. is the manipulation of actual darkness, not perceived darkness, which would entail in our minds.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good-Roll&quot;, which, I'm a bit Requiem tainted that a higher-gen., can't affect a lower-gen., no matter how good they roll, but as a ST, I'd say that whichever works for the story and, eight-dots is like, 5th gen, so, that's a very powerful character in a powerful game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'd say that the easier approach is to make &quot;all-powerful beings&quot; immune to such a thing, but then again in the story the NPC was in a weakened state, so I decided to allow him to be imprisoned, especially because it was interesting from a story perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}